From 3198040e655589014b1f687bbfd94f5f7b2d1d8f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 08:01:59 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] fix(ui): name the platform's command key in shortcut
 hints

The ribbon tips, operation-bar hints, machine-cell hover and the
cleared-toolpath status said Ctrl+Z / Ctrl+N ..., but the keyboard layer
binds egui's command modifier, which is Cmd on macOS. One helper
(shortcut_keys::chord) now builds every command-shortcut hint: Cmd on
macOS, Ctrl elsewhere. Ctrl+click pick hints stay Ctrl: those bindings
read the real Control modifier on every platform.

Fixes #1239

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX
