     assert!(model::find_by_name(&state.world, "Face1").is_some(), "the operation is kept");

From 415b2bd72727f5296b6a7605dca3cf1386368435 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 14:25:39 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix(ui): pick hints read the command key on macOS

The click-to-add pick hints (Edge mode hint, the "Click selects" hover,
the boundary pick help) said Ctrl, but the picks read mods.command
(Cmd on macOS, #1238). They now build the word through command_key() /
chord(); EDGE_HINT and boundary HINTS become fns. Adds the pure
command_key_for(macos) so both answers are tested on any host, and a
test pinning the three hints. Corrects the decision record, which
claimed those picks read mods.ctrl.

Refs #1239

